    "scope": "Prior policy evaluation on the exact loaded sources, using unchanged estimated_size; not an old executable run. Candidate domains are compared literally at caller epsilon capped at 1e-8. Test assertions separately cover images, topology, metadata, history and 3dm readback in both kernel feature modes."
  },
  "source_scope": "The baseline comparison evaluates the unchanged public estimated_size formula on the same loaded sources; the baseline Git call sites establish that it was the prior command policy. It is not a retained old-executable runtime comparison.",
  "coverage": [
    "The original explicit/trimmed/polysurface cases now require literal Automatic domain agreement as well as geometry, topology, attributes, groups, geometry text, history and 3dm readback.",
    "Fresh cases include weighted bilinear and quadratic patches, unclamped and split knots, rational changes of parameter, degree elevation, cones, sphere transposition, affine/anisotropic UV ranges, spatial scale, translation and common weight gauge.",
    "Raw single-surface targets match face-target results; zero-width requests preserve redo, and an interior collapsed sample remains supported.",
    "New quadrature and boundary-coincidence controls retain precise length/checkpoint behavior, large parameter origins, signed gauges and strict exact-collapse classification."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Inference and replay qualify the recorded inputs, not private Rhino implementation identity, continuous global Rhino equality, arbitrary conditioning or general performance.",
    "Numerical quadrature estimates have bounded resource use and estimated local error, not a rigorous continuous error certificate.",
    "Source/trim acceptance tolerances and general estimated_size remain independent; no C++/FFI changes or new ASan claim.",
    "Viewport face picking, block-instance copying and curved FilletSrf extension remain separate unfinished work."
  ],
